<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Siffin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">657 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-fitna">First Fitna</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Siffin was fought in 657 CE on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Ali and Mu'awiya, the governor of Syria, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-fitna">First Fitna</a>. The fighting ended inconclusively in arbitration, which divided Ali's supporters and led to the secession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharijites">Kharijites</a>. The battle deepened the civil war that brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> to an end.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-siffin.jpg" alt="Battle of Siffin" width="267" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sotheby's · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_Illustrated_and_Illuminated_leaf_from_a_Persian_Manuscript,_Persia,_Safavid,_dated_1516.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
